From 5e0595bb19e73256051cb748bac85fd516472330 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sun Yuechi <sunyuechi@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 14:31:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] osdc: fix ReplicaSplitOp chunk distribution and
 reassembly

ReplicaSplitOp::init_read() distributed chunks over a window of acting
indices starting at the random reference_sub_read and wrapping at the
OSD count. This broke reads in two ways:

- assemble_buffer_read() concatenates sub-read buffers in ascending
  acting-index order, but chunks were assigned in window order, so a
  wrapped window was reassembled in the wrong order.

- chunk_size rounded the division down, which can produce one more
  chunk than slice_count. The extra chunk wrapped the window fully
  around and attached a second read sharing one output buffer to the
  first sub-read.

Round the division up, and distribute the chunks over an explicit
window of valid acting indices assigned in ascending order.
init_reference_sub_read() now collects those indices and picks one of
them, matching ECSplitOp.

Signed-off-by: Sun Yuechi <sunyuechi@iscas.ac.cn>
---
 src/osdc/SplitOp.cc | 61 +++++++++++++++++++++++----------------------
 src/osdc/SplitOp.h  | 10 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/osdc/SplitOp.cc b/src/osdc/SplitOp.cc
index 7fbc65595442..962f537caad4 100644
--- a/src/osdc/SplitOp.cc
+++ b/src/osdc/SplitOp.cc
@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@
